1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
Zigzag Conversion — LeetCode 6

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,600
Problem: write the string in a zigzag across numRows rows, then read it back row by row.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,000
Example: "PAYPALISHIRING" over 3 rows reads out as "PAHNAPLSIIGYIR".

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,600
Key idea: don't compute any coordinates. Keep one text bucket per row.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,600
Drop each character into the current row, and bounce the direction at the top and bottom rows.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,600
cur starts at row 0 going down; it flips up at the last row and back down at row 0.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,600
Watch it fill: P down to row 0, A, Y to the bottom — then bounce up for P.

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:31,000
Keep going, zigzagging, and every character lands in exactly one row.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Now read it back: row 0 gives PAHN, row 1 gives APLSIIG, row 2 gives YIR.

10
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,000
Glue the rows top to bottom: "PAHNAPLSIIGYIR".

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,500
Time O(n), space O(n) for the row buckets — O(1) extra if you index each row directly.

12
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:48,000
